{"id":"73d916ed4bfd426c7ad85ceef5e6bdd39791c31e","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/druid","sha":"73d916ed4bfd426c7ad85ceef5e6bdd39791c31e","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/operations/metrics.md","lines":["@@ -479,6 +479,8 @@ These metrics are emitted by the Druid Coordinator in every run of the correspon"," |`tier/storage/capacity`|Total segment storage in bytes that each tier advertises for segment assignment. Can be greater than the physical disk reported by `tier/segmentCache/capacity` if using virtual storage, so use that metric rather than this one to monitor physical capacity. The `tierAlias` dimension is emitted only when the tier belongs to an alias configured via [`historicalTierAliases`](../configuration/index.md#dynamic-configuration).|`tier`, `tierAlias`|Varies|"," |`tier/segmentCache/capacity`|Total physical size in bytes of the segment cache locations configured on the historicals in each tier. The `tierAlias` dimension is emitted only when the tier belongs to an alias configured via [`historicalTierAliases`](../configuration/index.md#dynamic-configuration).|`tier`, `tierAlias`|Varies|"," |`tier/segmentCache/used`|Bytes occupied on disk in each tier by the segments its historicals have announced. Partially loaded segments count only the bytes the historical reported loading, not their full size. Compare against `tier/segmentCache/capacity` to see how full the tier's disks are. The `tierAlias` dimension is emitted only when the tier belongs to an alias configured via [`historicalTierAliases`](../configuration/index.md#dynamic-configuration).|`tier`, `tierAlias`|Varies|","+|`tier/segmentCache/utilization`|`tier/segmentCache/used` as a whole-number percentage of `tier/segmentCache/capacity`. Not emitted for a tier with no segment cache capacity. Can exceed 100 when a tier using virtual storage is assigned more than its disks hold. The `tierAlias` dimension is emitted only when the tier belongs to an alias configured via [`historicalTierAliases`](../configuration/index.md#dynamic-configuration).|`tier`, `tierAlias`|Varies|","+|`tierAlias/segmentCache/utilization`|Bytes occupied on disk across all tiers of an alias configured via [`historicalTierAliases`](../configuration/index.md#dynamic-configuration), as a whole-number percentage of their combined segment cache capacity. This is the overall fill of the alias and can sit well below its fullest tier, so to alert on a tier running out of disk use the maximum of `tier/segmentCache/utilization` grouped by `tierAlias`. Not emitted when no aliases are configured or when the alias's tiers have no segment cache capacity.|`tierAlias`|Varies|"," |`tier/required/capacity`|Deprecated. Use `tier/storage/required` instead, which reports the same value under a name that groups it with the storage capacity it should be compared against. This metric will be removed in a future release.|`tier`, `tierAlias`|Varies|"," |`tier/total/capacity`|Deprecated. Use `tier/storage/capacity` instead, which reports the same value under a name that groups it with the required storage it should be compared against. This metric will be removed in a future release.|`tier`, `tierAlias`|Varies|"," |`compact/task/count`|Number of tasks issued in the auto compaction run.| |Varies|"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions-contrib/prometheus-emitter/src/main/resources/defaultMetrics.json","lines":["@@ -193,6 +193,8 @@","   \"tier/storage/capacity\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Total segment storage in bytes available for assignment in each tier.\"},","   \"tier/segmentCache/capacity\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Total physical capacity in bytes of the segment cache locations in each tier.\"},","   \"tier/segmentCache/used\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Total bytes occupied on disk in each tier.\"},","+  \"tier/segmentCache/utilization\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Bytes occupied on disk in each tier as a whole-number percentage of its segment cache capacity.\"},","+  \"tierAlias/segmentCache/utilization\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Bytes occupied on disk across all tiers of each tier alias as a whole-number percentage of their combined segment cache capacity.\"},","   \"tier/required/capacity\" : { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Deprecated. Use tier/storage/required instead.\"},","   \"tier/total/capacity\" : { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Deprecated. Use tier/storage/capacity instead.\"},","   \"compact/task/count\" : { \"dimensions\" : [], \"type\" : \"gauge\", \"help\": \"Number of tasks issued in the auto compaction run.\"},"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions-contrib/statsd-emitter/src/main/resources/defaultMetricDimensions.json","lines":["@@ -187,6 +187,8 @@","   \"tier/storage/capacity\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\"},","   \"tier/segmentCache/capacity\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\"},","   \"tier/segmentCache/used\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\"},","+  \"tier/segmentCache/utilization\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\"},","+  \"tierAlias/segmentCache/utilization\": { \"dimensions\" : [\"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\"},","   \"tier/required/capacity\" : { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\" },","   \"tier/total/capacity\" : { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\" },","   \"tier/replication/factor\" : { \"dimensions\" : [\"tier\", \"tierAlias\"], \"type\" : \"gauge\" },"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"processing/src/main/resources/l